        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-05T04:06:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this method is called on some CS binder threads, but TcpKeepaliveController methods are not thread-safe: should we grab a lock here ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 458,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 458,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "5c9740683aa1df10efc9c229c27deeffc9a2f7ee",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f326ba65_3d0be6f2",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/KeepaliveTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 458,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-05T11:43:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That doesn\u0027t help. In a way you can see the file descriptor update as atomic ; the problem is one of ordering. This method lobs a message to the service handler, so the issue would be the handler thread not seeing this already done. I think at most the probability of this happening is very small. However, it looks very possible that this gets called twice before the message arrives.\n\nIn any case, this should absolutely not be done here, but after the message is received. Added a TODO.",
      "parentUuid": "d422530b_cec5988c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 458,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 458,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "5c9740683aa1df10efc9c229c27deeffc9a2f7ee",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
